6,Yazghulami language — Grokipedia,https://grokipedia.com/page/yazghulami_language,"Yazghulami (also known as Yazgulyami or Zǵamiǵai; ISO 639-3: yah) is an Eastern Iranian language belonging to the Southeastern branch of the Indo-Iranian language family, specifically within the Pamir subgroup of Pamir languages. [1][2] It is spoken primarily by the Yazghulami people along the Yazgulyam River in the Rushan District of Tajikistan's Gorno-Badakhshan Autonomous Region, in the ...",Yazghulami,Indo-European
